Notebook[{
Cell["A Working Tour of the `Symmetry` Sub-Context", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"9cd12c7c-a61f-4013-8f79-e1e21189c283"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This tutorial walks through every function the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Wolfram"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "faf2f695-2407-42ef-9366-915d44bc2f90"],
 "TensorNetworks",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Symmetry"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "96a3015b-0d7e-4ce5-bd83-718b4b1ea6ff"],
 "` sub-context exports, in the order a tensor-network practitioner actually \
meets them. The goal is operational: after working through the document you \
should be able to (i) decide whether a partition or a tableau is the right \
object for a problem, (ii) predict the size of every block of a \
symmetry-resolved tensor in closed form, and (iii) project a real TN tensor \
onto the irrep subspace it physically belongs to. Every claim below is paired \
with a small Wolfram Language cell that you can rerun and modify; nothing is \
asserted without being computed."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8305b44f-6773-4596-85b0-608d2d719366"],

Cell["\<\
We start where the physics starts: two indistinguishable particles. From \
there we walk up the ladder of rank, picking up one Symmetry-subcontext \
function per pedagogical step. By the end we will have used all twelve \
exported functions, every one of them at least once on a tensor that has a \
tensor-network reason to exist.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0e213f00-bb1c-4824-930d-ad33d246de02"],

Cell["Inventory", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b80e6d17-31bc-4bd7-b527-94ebf28a0fa2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The sub-context exports twelve symbols. Six are about the ",
 StyleBox["combinatorics", "TI"],
 " of Young diagrams (a counting layer that decides \"how much room is there?\
\"). Six are about the ",
 StyleBox["action on tensors", "TI"],
 " (the operational layer that produces a tensor in the right symmetry class)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10d788f4-113d-46a4-ad5b-61aa263d294d"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Symbol", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"faa9ab25-0a85-41f0-9d1b-868ce6a02024"],
     Cell["Layer", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"516a9a3c-f1cd-4964-82bc-649a34e2d835"],
     Cell["One-line role", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"6f91309e-4211-4fbc-b914-38187797d73c"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "PartitionQ"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "2fa20506-737c-4a0a-8a18-ee5730739547"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "9c3b758a-7f03-4fa4-98dd-71cb0fcdbbe4"], Cell[
    "combinatorics", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "cb857fd4-bea7-41d2-9822-99e219bd2cd0"], Cell[
    "Is this list a valid Young-diagram shape?", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "b1d0505d-421d-48f8-bf2b-8262625e6b82"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "TransposePartition"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "470facf5-85a9-48ae-98dc-30cd83dea22f"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7de1c47e-f90c-431f-a9f2-23520e0e1e3e"], Cell[
    "combinatorics", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "ac32c17b-4102-48ff-a600-07526e892437"], Cell[
    "Swap rows and columns of the diagram.", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "b321738f-cfbc-4cc1-9471-5ed8c42d6dd5"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "YoungTableau"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "e9e584cd-b749-4cda-ac3f-9a7df934074b"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6feabc38-0e0a-4119-938e-6ee921f672f6"], Cell[
    "combinatorics", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6852345e-aed6-4033-ad9d-1029696eac93"], Cell[
    "Wrap a diagram (with slot labels) into a typed object.", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"17a3150f-a359-4f2b-97e7-b5a72f2992ca"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "YoungTableauQ"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "d5ec5c29-4d59-4d64-b9e3-bf776876663a"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "fae37a55-8f26-4b30-add9-19a022023934"], Cell[
    "combinatorics", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "3fae9e35-f73e-469c-8ac9-85d9c6e2fbcf"], Cell[TextData[{
     "Is this ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"YoungTableau", "[", "...", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
      ExpressionUUID->"19abb7d3-07b6-4052-a629-51eb391914d1"],
     " well-formed?"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"384ffffa-7930-4d06-aa75-f828441f1b79"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "TableauShape"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "56deac2c-bf27-4cda-87f4-652a8359a704"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "299b5ba8-727f-41f0-bd05-bd223ea73ba1"], Cell[
    "combinatorics", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "18c4c9ce-bcbb-4ce7-8ed1-9950acb862c6"], Cell[
    "Read off the partition from a tableau.", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "77fe71aa-9e18-45a4-b44f-a0fabc7b8872"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "TableauSize"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "8a9c328e-536d-4d1b-b367-1a67a529b480"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0adf8a1c-ee38-4315-9975-dac7e220b863"], Cell[
    "combinatorics", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "e007101a-de58-439f-9e70-c415b4625860"], Cell[TextData[{
     "Total box count ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "851a706f-e392-4715-8221-c59718940303"],
     " (the rank we will act on)."
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6b53ca35-e2df-4fb4-8804-15279ddd74b6"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "HookLength"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "6fb1edeb-f72a-4017-be64-c07096ef2293"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "f075d046-5b66-4754-aaa4-f82c24a2126b"], Cell[
    "dimensions", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "59222ef1-ed2f-41a2-befd-28d2fdfd64bb"], Cell[
    "One cell's hook length.", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5719215e-e357-4d5b-a9eb-07e5de68e193"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "HookLengths"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "876ed9e9-5580-41a6-90f3-a2915c2faf20"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "e8284dd4-cf5d-45b1-8128-e5b3c4d9b176"], Cell[
    "dimensions", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "477a57db-89ed-4194-b050-3bbcafb63804"], Cell[
    "All hook lengths in one nested list.", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "e503576f-f93c-45a9-93f2-d90c4f2d23b3"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "HookFactor"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "73d18b86-0dcc-4c6d-9525-c944b23e5030"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4ab32f2a-1109-43e8-87da-52a2a3a3c564"], Cell[
    "dimensions", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "ea070284-82aa-4e47-8eb9-fb489608fc01"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "\[Product]", 
        StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      ExpressionUUID->"3c97f377-93b7-49c4-9d10-037e95bdf106"],
     ", the prefactor in the dimension formula."
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"43831e87-79e0-4346-9815-4fcea97dca74"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "TableauDimension"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "747cba0a-4019-43bf-9bb0-530e56647ce8"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "1af00e42-e613-4411-a5be-72e64f310668"], Cell[
    "dimensions", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2661ff43-4386-4dd2-9b0c-71055fddaf2a"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"dim", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Lambda]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
      "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8136642e-9f89-4dc9-a7ae-05445b7d8c8a"],
     
     ", the irrep dimension."
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"49772937-a579-4f31-9702-6de2fc5d2d8f"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "YoungSymmetrize"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "b9f18672-0ff1-4212-98f4-bf896537297e"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "f188f5f4-306b-4a94-be89-02ce170a39eb"], Cell[
    "tensor action", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "8269d81d-f5c2-4cd0-9bd3-fcd95d44eb14"], Cell[TextData[{
     "Unnormalised Young symmetriser ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "\[CenterDot]", 
        StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      ExpressionUUID->"62794fb5-abb8-42d4-a710-bd5c146237c3"],
     "."
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0514f1cd-cb1f-4fb9-abec-5bc3fc8524e0"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "YoungProject"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "bd66a922-da62-4b8b-941d-adf9f9afc183"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6e533906-1660-472f-8332-c827ae2b9ac5"], Cell[
    "tensor action", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "a71aea30-a2a8-4e5d-b137-d973b028f3e3"], Cell[TextData[{
     "Idempotent projector ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[Lambda]"], "/", 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}], ")"}], " ", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      ExpressionUUID->"4e500066-23c2-4908-bea3-b11038340077"],
     "."
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"034c03f4-6990-4b28-a53f-d6a004f7df68"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}]], "TableNotes",\
ExpressionUUID->"b22c87b2-2ef7-43a5-bdbb-875d76ab9ac8"],

Cell["\<\
The tutorial is structured around four physical settings that successively \
bring more of these functions into play:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f37dd193-5703-4592-8629-24c25b280abc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Two-site bonds and identical particles",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungTableau"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5d0340b0-3f8f-486d-8fa5-6f847b62e8c9"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungTableauQ"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f0f53340-e2b5-4013-a2c6-4532de5e3f09"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "TableauShape"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "bafb5057-451d-4cf9-bb53-e64b5d4f9486"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "TableauSize"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d2887088-40cd-4caf-9e0f-d1dd54ca3b8d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungSymmetrize"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1cba50b4-9005-43e1-9895-2e81bea941b5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungProject"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4221c24c-acac-4fe9-8a15-07ef4e5d91b1"],
 "."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"b8cdeab1-61af-4a46-8d4b-2c1499cc807c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Diagrams as combinatorial bookkeeping",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " picks up ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "PartitionQ"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "31525540-892d-49f2-902f-0b26d6116954"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "TransposePartition"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5f156da3-0648-49c4-bef2-c5a6159571e0"],
 "."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"f338491a-fd50-4d9c-8fde-43565c49b7d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Counting before allocating",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " brings in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "HookLength"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "542e99dc-62d5-48fd-8da9-9bbb4a89cd10"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "HookLengths"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9fee097b-337d-4ad7-86c2-0df66cb2dd23"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "HookFactor"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9e0e1e8b-5d7d-432c-b7ef-7d52bc9c09fd"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "TableauDimension"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8ce828ea-5b46-4e78-9ed2-8bb77897ffb5"],
 "."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"defac7ea-7712-4b28-b6a6-cbf87f6ff1ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Three TN payoffs",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " revisits every function in working examples: Schur-Weyl block \
decomposition on three sites, the Riemann tensor as a rank-4 TN node, and the \
spectrum of a class-function Hamiltonian via content sums."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"6e836fda-1c22-49dc-b2f2-d31aafef77d1"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c36ff257-c4af-4c13-8c53-668885208fbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Load the paclet and pull the sub-context into scope. From this point every \
code cell in the tutorial assumes these two ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Needs"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "966c6e9e-e741-47e8-aaec-61f6a2c72088"],
 " have been run."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"782b17b2-cad6-473f-b32b-e1949300e782"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/TensorNetworks\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`TensorNetworks`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`TensorNetworks`Symmetry`\>\"", "]"}], 
   ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"10", "^", 
    RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c68fdef7-dbf9-4e54-914f-d5615f1a1fa4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
 "tol"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5f40ff7c-959e-4cbd-af72-7738b7bc2531"],
 " will be our numerical tolerance for \"is this tensor identity satisfied?\" \
checks."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e601bdc-6a1b-4e61-b812-9aa9ee78321c"],

Cell["1. Two indistinguishable particles on a bond", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"b3ed5dda-60b9-4a38-8bb8-14cee952649d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Picture the simplest non-trivial tensor in a tensor network: a rank-2 node ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"434311e5-a451-4028-88ee-72573eb38813"],
 " on a bond between two physical sites, with each index ranging over a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "11886bc1-ec6a-4855-9877-990c5ef9034f"],
 "-dimensional local Hilbert space ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "18857948-ec22-4111-968c-833443d947e1"],
 ". So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8930b76b-34ef-4e35-a432-07ed89b73b3e"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b2559868-59ec-4ae1-9abe-d858a508e0db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If the two sites carry ",
 StyleBox["identical", "TI"],
 " particles, quantum mechanics demands a definite parity under exchange. \
Bosons sit in the symmetric square ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Sym",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d74f834b-9577-4182-a09c-504064a119b5"],
 ", fermions in the antisymmetric square ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", "2"], 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "95620dff-684b-4428-8bc4-81ea05e512ca"],
 ". A generic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "49047fcd-44fe-4189-89b7-0aab5459803d"],
 " is neither; it is a sum of a symmetric and an antisymmetric piece, and you \
must project onto the one your physics calls for before doing anything else \
with the tensor."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e3ad2ff-44a5-4105-83ae-dbd3d5074c21"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Concretely, write a generic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2803a3dd-eb43-42bd-bf7a-42ac74f3b4dc"],
 " with symbolic entries:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"64e421fc-2de0-4288-8e05-7d9a8d6e0ce7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"T", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"75d3fbad-4ab8-4ff3-9cfd-ecda8b2b9241"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bosonic projection is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6174915e-43ed-4389-9433-44132bf1a0f8"],
 "; the fermionic projection is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"75c450ac-8e21-4272-9441-25784efac0fe"],
 ". We could write those by hand, but the Symmetry sub-context lets us name \
them by their ",
 StyleBox["symmetry class", "TI"],
 " and apply the right operator without spelling out which transposition to \
take. That naming is what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungTableau"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "165093a8-2ec9-4066-83c9-393ead950fc1"],
 " is for."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"939e8b4f-a83e-44dc-903c-3e4b994551ae"],

Cell["`YoungTableau`: the named handle for a symmetry class", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1cd59d5d-b85b-48a7-a690-ab4e61959da3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["Young tableau", "TI"],
 " is a left-justified arrangement of boxes (the \"shape\") together with a \
labelling of those boxes by the slot indices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"75949f7c-21cb-4de3-9663-07302f7c2331"],
 " of the tensor we plan to act on. For two indices there are exactly two \
shapes:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"741f08bc-f6c6-42fd-90e1-0e1ca114148f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "one row of two boxes, written ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1a0ddf6e-2984-414e-aa3d-66b6c4a53682"],
 ", labels the ",
 StyleBox["symmetric", "TI"],
 " class;"
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0f31a8bc-e7c3-4c01-856c-1dcdbe30f7ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "one column of two boxes, written ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"32671136-fb93-4946-a0ca-7a66db2567ed"],
 ", labels the ",
 StyleBox["antisymmetric", "TI"],
 " class."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4095db04-246d-4985-be7f-9365a1cba7aa"],

Cell["Build the two tableaux:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"71c8958f-c544-44f2-8876-e45c62411649"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"symTab", "  ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"YoungTableau", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"antiTab", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"YoungTableau", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"dbaaa869-a22f-41ef-9faf-60098a07a64d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each call returns a typed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"YoungTableau", "[", "...", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c8beb541-a690-4d34-8508-b1567e09fd0d"],
 " object with a summary display. The constructor accepts two forms. We just \
used the ",
 StyleBox["partition", "TI"],
 " form, in which the argument is a non-increasing list of row lengths and \
the slot labels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d33c5543-bc42-4980-8472-9199a834dbaa"],
 " are filled in row by row. The other form takes the rows of slot labels \
explicitly:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9de2a4a3-d6d8-46c1-978e-e856e9d7a68f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
